---
import LetsTalk from '@components/home/LetsTalk.astro'
import Insight from '@components/insights/Insight.astro'
import { siteConfig } from '@config/site'
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="Why and When To Do A Discovery Phase"
  description="A short insight on the importance and timing of a discovery phase in project development."
>
  <Insight>
    <span slot="insight-title">Why and When To Do A Discovery Phase</span>
    <span slot="insight-text">
      <p>
        The purpose of a <a href="/services/discovery" class="underline underline-offset-2">discovery phase</a> is to gather
        information, clarify objectives, and identify potential risks before starting a project. It helps ensure that everyone
        involved has a clear understanding of the project's goals, target audience, and requirements. A discovery phase can
        involve activities such as workshops, stakeholder interviews, market/user research, competitive analysis, and more.
      </p><br />
      <p>
        If your project is not large or complex, and you already have a clear understanding (plus documentation) of
        these, then in all honesty a full discovery phase is probably not necessary. Instead, a shorter scoping meeting
        or workshop may be sufficient to align yourself and your chosen developer on objectives and scope.
      </p><br />
      <p>
        However, if your project is large or complex, then you need a discovery phase that is tailored to your project's
        specific needs and you should be wary of anyone that wants to jump straight into design or development without
        understanding the full context.
      </p><br />
      <p>
        Still have questions? Give us a <a href={`tel:${siteConfig.phone}`} class="underline underline-offset-2">call</a
        > or
        <a href="/contact" class="underline underline-offset-2">send us a message</a> to understand more without any pushy
        sales tactics.
      </p>
    </span>
  </Insight>

  <LetsTalk />
</Layout>
